{title: 442 - How Sweet Are the Tidings}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Early Advent}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Gb]How sweet [Db]are the tidings that [Gb]greet the [Db/Ab]pilgrim's [Ab7]ear,
[Ab7]As he wanders [Db]in exile from home!
[Db]Soon, soon will the Savior in glory appear,
[Bbm]And soon will the kingdom [Ab]come.

Refrain:
[Db]He's coming, coming, coming soon I know,
[Db]Coming [Gb]back to [Db/Ab]this earth again;
[Ab]And the weary pilgrims [Db]will to [Gb]glory go,
[Gb]When the Savior [Db]comes to reign.

Verse 2:
[Gb]The mossy [Db]old graves where [Gb]the pilgrims [Ab7]sleep
[Ab7]Shall be open [Db]as wide as before,
[Db]And the millions that sleep in the mighty deep
[Bbm]Shall live on this earth once [Ab]more.

Verse 3:
[Gb]There we'll [Db]meet ne'er to part [Gb]in our [Db/Ab]happy
[Ab7]Eden home, Sweet [Db]songs of redemption we'll sing;
[Db]From the north, from the south, all the ransomed shall come,
[Bbm]And worship our heavenly [Ab]King.

Verse 4:
[Gb]Hallelujah, [Db/Ab]Amen! Hallelujah [Ab7]again!
[Ab7]Soon, if faithful, [Db]we all shall be there;
[Db]O, be watchful, be hopeful, be joyful till then,
[Bbm]And a crown of bright glory [Ab]we'll wear.
